      "why": "The spec requires 32 results/us throughput and a 0.44us p99 batch latency for 32 simultaneous requests. Only the pipelined family (1 result/cycle) can meet the throughput constraint (>=32 Msps) without requiring an unrealistically high Fmax. Iterative and unrolled_k produce 1 result every N or N/k cycles, making 32 Msps throughput impossible at reasonable Fmax. Pipelined_m also gives 1 result/cycle but has higher latency (ceil(N/m)+2) and more area than pipelined for the same N, so it is less likely to be on the Pareto front for this area-minimizing objective. The accuracy constraint (max_abs_err <= 2^-12) requires sufficient n_iter and data_width; CORDIC error is dominated by the residual angle after N iterations, so n_iter >= 12 is needed for 12-bit accuracy. data_width 14-18 covers the range where output LSB (2^-(W-2)) is at or below 2^-12 (W>=14) with some margin for angle_guard and frac_guard effects. angle_guard 0-2 and frac_guard 0-2 are kept small to minimize area while still allowing the angle path to converge. Rounding is included as a choice since it affects accuracy at the margin."
